# Chief of Staff daily briefing — YOUR customization.
#
# TEMPLATE: copy to briefing.yaml and customize.
# The real briefing.yaml is machine-local and gitignored — it may contain
# personal standing requests and must NEVER be committed to a public repo.
#
# Edit freely; it syncs to your CoS server and shapes every morning's briefing.

# Sections to include, in order. The CoS fills each with real content.
sections:
  - good_morning     # health: readiness, sleep, HRV, capacity
  - the_world        # what moved: news + market, tied to your work
  - the_ask          # decisions that need YOUR verdict today
  - focus            # 3-5 things that deserve your attention
  - priority_pulse   # are your priorities moving or stalled?
  - delegate         # what agents handle tonight
  - watch            # aging/at-risk items
  - observation      # the CoS's narrative read of the day

# Standing requests — the CoS honors every one, every day.
# Add your own; these are instructions, not suggestions.
additions:
  - "Example: always call out <project> status if there's any movement or block."
  - "Example: end with a one-line summary in a specific tone or voice."
